      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Error is generated only when TCPM send SOP* message and it is shorter than 2 bytes. If different message is sent (e.g. hard reset) than body of the message is not important and can be 0 or 1 byte. So it is not checking if type is correct, but if message length is correct for particular message type.\n2. `NUM_SOP_STAR_TYPES` is defined as `TCPCI_MSG_SOP_DEBUG_PRIME_PRIME + 1`, so I think that `\u003c` is correct to filter only SOP* types.",
